# Text files are LF in every checkout, Windows included. Git for Windows installs with
# core.autocrlf=true, so without this a default clone there -- and the windows-latest runner the
# git-bash CI job uses -- checks the scripts out CRLF, and every fixture that patches or matches a
# checked-out file line by line reads a `\r` it never wrote (ludics-lite#318).
* text=auto eol=lf
